<p class="fact">Proposals, for discussion only: (1) the ${industryCands.filter((c) => c.m.sound && !adoptedTop.has(c.label.toLowerCase())).length} sound FMP industries with no adopted cohort leading in them are the first candidates, because they are pure by construction and the tree already knows every member; (2) a registry cohort marked weak for 'the names disagree' is not wrong — it may be a theme, not a business — but its mean should not be drawn until it passes; (3) the Hub tabs BLUE CHIP, LARGE CAP, MEGA CAP and GROWTH are size and style filters, not businesses, and read as filters (the registry already files BLUE_CHIP that way); (4) off-Hub members can only join a cohort where the close Geiger reads them (it reads ${SC.rows.length} names), and today only ${names.filter((n) => !n.served).length} such names are on the tree. Nothing above was written to a table, a view, a row or the registry.</p>

