<details class="sc-pagespecs"><summary>PAGE SPECS</summary><p>This report and the gallery beside it (index.html) were built by build.mjs from committed inputs only: the live tree's tree.json and industry-20261002.json (origin/hub/release-20260923 @9d2b1ca), the T10 design sheet (data/tree-standard-t10.json, copied from the held branch hub/t10-tree-standard-20261002 @e133a81), today's reads of the chart API (data/hub-geiger-20261003.json = the live Hub Geiger at ${esc(G.computed_utc)}; data/scout-geiger-20261003.json = the close Geiger as of ${esc(SC.as_of)}; data/universe-20261003.json = the ${UNI.count} served lines), read-only snapshots of public.cohort_registry, public.cohorts (the board's tabs), public.ticker_membership, public.ticker_cohorts and the six closes of the tree's names from massive_stocks.scout_geiger_daily (data/*.json, read with supabase db query, nothing written), Alan's lists as read on 2 Oct (deliverables/20261002/served-set-v2/data/universe-and-lists.json: favorites ${LISTS.favorites.length}, liked ${LISTS.liked.length}, radar ${LISTS.radar.length}), and the measurements of one headless run of the live page at 1920 × 1080 (proof-parts.mjs → shots/parts-proof-A.json, parts-proof-B.json: every box and label rectangle, the panels, the camera distance, the black share of the canvas as the share of its pixels at most 22 in every channel). The cohort measures are plain means and standard errors; the soundness rule (n ≥ 8, standard error ≤ 0.10, held on 6 closes, biggest industry ≥ 60 % or fund-defined) is the same tolerance the served-set standard uses (±0.1 at the close) and is a proposal for discussion, not a rule applied anywhere. The price and day change on the gallery's label part are the card's live values at the time of the run. What could be wrong: the close Geiger reads 3 rungs and the Hub's 7, so a cohort mixing on-Hub and off-Hub names mixes two readings (each row says which); a Hub tab's members are the board's tickers today and may differ from what the tree calls that cohort; the first view's pixels-per-unit depends on the canvas height (998 px here, under an 82 px header). What was not done: no screenshot of a phone or of the MacBook at scale 2 (the brief asked for 1920 × 1080 only); the coil component is lane V2's and is linked, not drawn; nothing was deployed, merged or written to the Hub.</p></details>
